                <pb facs="0426" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 186.3411/108: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander of United States Naval Forces in the
                        Eastern Mediterranean</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullard</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Admiral W. S. Benson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fiume</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-23">December 23,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Adriatic 30. Unpleasant incident occurred at Spalato between Italian destroyer
                    Carabiniere and Slav population. Leading Jugo-Slav citizens and Serbian officers
                    prevented disorder. Have reports which will communicate to Italian Admiral at
                    Sebenico. Entirely local and no further consequences expected but is typical of
                    feeling between two nations.</p>
                <p>First meeting Naval Inquiry Committee December 22.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
